WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.820
So Ra No Wo To

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.960
There we go!

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:02.470
It's fall now.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:07.430
A Typhoon Passes - Illusion and Reality

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:11.810
So your dad was a tanker?

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:12.590
That's right.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:13.920
He was one of the
legendary heroes

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.340
who led over a thousand
citizens and soldiers

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:20.510
out of the surrounded
city of Wardenburk

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.580
in just six Type-2 Millipads!

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.220
Amazing.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.370
Isn't it?

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:32.090
And when he was wounded
in battle,

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:36.090
he met my mother, who was a medic
at the hospital he went to.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:41.530
And you ended up their kid.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:42.910
Yup!

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.090
Am I a potato?

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:50.230
My! What a wonderful potato...

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.110
You took such good care
of them, Kana-chan.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:59.860
We'll be able to share some
with the townspeople.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.900
Oh, Claus-san is coming, too.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.020
Maybe we'll give him
some as a present.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:07.410
He's coming?

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:11.340
You really like him, don't you?

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.150
I-It isn't that I like him...

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.440
I respect him.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.420
Poke.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.780
Rio-sempai...

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.660
I didn't know she could do that.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.760
She's really good!

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:56.790
The wind's started to blow.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:02.700
The weather's going to get bad soon.
We should go inside.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:03.500
Right!

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:04.340
Right!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.520
You, too, Noël-chan.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.690
Like...

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.890
Isn't something strange
about Rio-sempai?

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.400
How so?

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.070
The way she was playing
that trumpet?

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.610
Wasn't that wonderful?

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.950
She's so cool.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.870
She seems kind of down.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.140
Rio-sempai never talks
more than she has to.

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.330
But... I know! Dinner!

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.100
That tempura was
good, wasn't it?

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.670
Yup! The potatoes
were so crisp...

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:41.710
That's not it!

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:49.790
Here you go, Rio.
Eat up while it's hot.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.310
Thanks.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:56.880
Is it good?

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:57.850
Yeah.

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:58.640
I see.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.010
I'm glad.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:06.170
She was scarfing down
the green peppers!

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.530
Rio-sempai, eating peppers?

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:09.340
That's right!

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:12.460
No matter how chopped-up
they are,

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.500
Rio-sempai always finds the peppers
and takes them out!

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.850
Well...

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.500
That could be bad.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:31.890
Poke.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.710
Is this Claus-san?

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:43.990
Yeah! It's my treasure!

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.360
The Desert Wolf, Miracle Claus!

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:51.290
On his left breast, a wolf's head
tattoo symbolizes the glory

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:52.950
and unity of the 481st platoon!

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:55.300
Isn't it cool?

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:56.710
You can't have it.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.710
Don't worry too much, OK?

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:07.470
The thing with the captain was
overthinking on our parts.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.640
'Cause it's Rio-sempai!

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.350
She's cool, awesome,
and so pretty.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:17.920
Yeah!

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:22.740
I'm sure she conquered her hatred of green
peppers and can eat them now.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:26.670
Kureha-chan, you really
like her, don't you?

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.930
She's the person I look up to!

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:34.370
Me, too, but...
What do you think, Noël-chan?

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:42.710
Poke...

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:43.750
Watch out!

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:57.140
Noël-chan's asleep.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:01.590
Oh, well. She can have
half my bed, I guess.

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:03.780
Kanata, you grab that end.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.150
OK!

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:24.990
You forgot to turn off
the fire in the bath.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:27.500
Sorry. I wasn't thinking.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:33.050
The way you seem so on top of things, but actually
aren't, is one of your charm points.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:36.010
But lately, there's been
too much of that.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.520
I'm sorry.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:43.810
Do you regret hanging
up on your father?

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.740
It can't be helped, I guess.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:53.120
I'll cover for your problems
with your job.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:08:01.120
At least be an awesome sempai
when they're around, OK?

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.480
Is that the wind?

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.440
No.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:12.940
Sorry for dropping by so late.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:14.220
It's a Class-1 Priority.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:15.680
Who's it for?

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:20.530
Master Sergeant Rio Kazumiya
of the 1121 Platoon.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:25.100
Please take it.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:36.530
Major, come in.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:41.500
Even the Desert Wolf couldn't
go anywhere in this rain.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:45.040
I told you not to call me that.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.000
I'm sorry.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:50.500
As an apology, how about
some hot tea and a bath?

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:58.140
Thank you for completing your
mission in this typhoon!

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:03.020
I'm sorry all we have is
leftovers from dinner.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.020
Here you go.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:11.780
You should've woken me
up when he got here!

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:18.240
These are good!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.530
It's even good cold.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.710
The green peppers
are quality, too.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:23.090
Really?

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:26.250
I was the one who picked
and fried them!

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.250
You'll be quite a wife someday.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.630
Is that a new paper?

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.820
Yes, the Major brought
it with him.

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:39.820
How are the peace talks?

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:42.770
The conference isn't going well.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.930
Neither side's conditions
are being met...

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:50.310
If Princess Iliya were still alive,
things might be different.

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:54.610
Princess Iliya...

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:59.340
You don't know her?
She was the hero of Vingt!

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:02.530
The first princess of
Archduke Arkadia!

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:05.410
She's the Helvetian army's
goddess of victory!

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:09.950
She's a tanker goddess, right up there
with Claus the Desert Wolf!

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:12.170
Kureha, that's actually-

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:14.630
Is everyone here?

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.300
There's an emergency!

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:33.300
Rio!

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.300
Rio!

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.870
What's going on?

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:49.800
One of Yumina's kids has
been missing all day.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:51.070
Help us look!

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:51.790
What?

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.300
Yumina-san, who vanished?

00:10:57.370 --> 00:10:58.840
Seiya-san.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.450
The river's risen quite a bit.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:17.490
The fields downstream haven't
been harvested yet.

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:20.660
If the dam breaks, they're all done for.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:22.530
I've never been to the city.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.210
Show me around, Kureha.

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:25.430
OK!

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:28.790
I'm really sorry.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.000
I only took my eyes off
him for a second...

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:34.240
Search and rescue
is an army's job.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:35.500
Leave it to us.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:43.100
Let's go.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:44.010
Right!

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:50.380
Seiya!

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:52.740
Seiya-san!

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:03.900
Wow. There's so much water...

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:06.530
If he fell...

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:14.800
Seiya!

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:16.800
Seiya-san!

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:22.970
What?

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:23.970
You!

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.720
You know something, don't you?

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:32.220
You came out here because you
have some idea where he is!

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.280
Tell me!

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:36.240
Where is Seiya?

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:40.650
The fields...

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:41.740
The fields?

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.860
Yumina-oneechan loves eggplants.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:50.240
So everyone used their
allowances and...

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.370
Seiya must've...

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:55.210
Where is it?

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:21.390
What's wrong with you?

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:24.570
What are you doing, downriver
in the middle of a typhoon?

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.280
I must protect the eggplants!

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:27.710
What?

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:28.820
You idiot!

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:31.120
Everyone's risking their
lives for you!

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:32.810
No one asked you to come!

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:34.480
I didn't ask for help!

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.800
What?!

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:38.710
Stop being such a brat!

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.150
Listen...

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:50.160
Kids without parents have to be stronger
than those who have them.

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:54.050
When you cause trouble for people,
you're not the only one they get angry at.

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:58.750
They get mad at Yumina.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.820
Your big sister, too.

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:03.820
Kureha...

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:06.320
OK.

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.900
I'm an orphan, too. So I know.

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:14.500
Now, let's get back.

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:16.410
But...

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.280
Are you going to keep whining?

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:19.710
Hold up.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:23.530
When you've worked really
hard to raise something,

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:27.270
you value it the same
as your own life.

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:33.260
These are big enough
to be eaten.

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:38.560
They'll be great pickled.

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.030
Thanks, mister!

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:45.500
Major...

00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:57.740
Seiya-kun's started going back up.

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.370
Major, go on ahead!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:20.560
N-No... You go first.

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:22.950
Leave the rear to me.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:24.320
OK!

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.890
They're both safe.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.200
But...

00:15:57.310 --> 00:16:00.070
Now, they have no way
to get back up.

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:03.270
This is really bad...

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:12.450
Thank you.

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:15.990
The situation is bad.

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:19.290
But you're with me!

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:23.220
I believe we'll be OK.

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:27.590
You're wrong...

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.670
Did you say something?

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.000
No...

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:38.300
Listen, don't be afraid.

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:41.680
You're with Miracle Claus now!

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.050
Right!

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:46.150
The ground's starting to collapse!

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:48.090
The flooding's making the
ground crumble...

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:51.880
Damn! This is why I hate kids!

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:56.510
Kids who don't listen should just be tied
up and locked in a room somewhere!

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:57.790
Rio!

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.550
What good will scaring them do?

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:05.350
You know they're always
watching you.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:09.760
I'm sorry... That was too far.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.140
B-But I'm sure it'll be all right.

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:15.840
Claus-san is supposed to
be a miracle worker.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:17.060
That's not true.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:23.280
He's not the Desert Wolf
or Miracle Claus.

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:28.260
He just happens to have the same name
and close to the same appearance.

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:33.660
When they first met, Kureha just decided
it on her own and got all happy...

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:36.010
You know how he doesn't
really talk much, right?

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:39.810
He just never found the
right time to tell her...

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:41.700
But...

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:46.450
Anyway, we need to think of how
to save those two down there:

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:49.990
the courier with years of
service but nothing else,

00:17:49.990 --> 00:17:53.030
and the one with tons of enthusiasm,
but no experience.

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:56.080
Give them a rope?

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.750
There's no good spot above them.

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:02.350
And it's too far to send
it from here.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:06.820
There is a way to get
them the rope.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:08.770
There.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:13.090
The first time I met you,

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:18.340
I thought my dad would have been
like you if he were still alive.

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:24.790
I tell everyone that I knew
my dad really well,

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:30.560
but it's all second-hand information.
I don't actually know much.

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:34.570
He died when I was very little.

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:35.870
Kureha...

00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:03.740
Watch the upper left?

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:12.700
Pull! Pull! Pull!

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:07.330
The Takemikazuchi!

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:13.980
Stop!

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:18.840
Noël-chan, how is it?

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:22.270
Linear Anchoring Coil online.

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:26.220
Targeting System partially
online from B7 to F5.

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:27.730
Initiating targeting.

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:36.230
It can be shot.

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:39.240
Prepare to fire the wire anchor!

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:40.960
Kanata, do it!

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.000
Right!

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:52.990
It's coming!

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:59.590
I'll protect you, in your late father's place!

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:05.010
Right... Major...

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:10.270
Ready! Fire!

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:17.370
Come here!

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:20.570
Kureha!

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.170
Major!

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:31.080
Kureha-chan!

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.520
Pull up the anchor!

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:33.750
Hurry!

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:04.710
Hey, Kureha...

00:21:04.710 --> 00:21:08.030
We're safe now, so I'll tell you...

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:09.050
I-

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:11.110
I knew it.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.810
You are the person I admire!

00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:32.100
The blue sky after a typhoon, huh?

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:33.970
So you kept it up the whole time?

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:35.820
Honestly, I'm surprised.

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:38.020
I didn't think you could do it.

00:21:38.490 --> 00:21:41.250
When I saw her eyes,
her total faith in me,

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:45.240
I was more scared of breaking
her dreams than of dying.

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:49.540
That's why I was able to do it.

00:21:50.770 --> 00:21:54.000
In the end, I guess I'm a coward.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:55.650
That's not true!

00:21:55.650 --> 00:21:57.580
You're wonderful, Claus-san!

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.540
Listen up, miss.

00:22:00.970 --> 00:22:05.290
Most of the time, what you
think you see in a person

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:07.800
and what they're really
feeling are different.

00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:12.940
Admiring someone always
makes your vision blurry.

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:18.170
Someday, when you're looked at
in that way, you'll understand.

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:22.310
Are you sure you can't stay
until she wakes up?

00:22:22.930 --> 00:22:25.070
Can you tell her for me?

00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:32.330
That this is the most honorable
wound I've ever received!

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:19.890
A Departure - The First Snow

00:24:15.750 --> 00:24:16.430
Next time:

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:17.400
A Departure.

00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:19.340
The First Snow.

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:24.930
This program is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to people, parties,
or situations is purely coincidental.
